# A second net under the "files" allowlist in package.json.
#
# Note what this file cannot do: npm gives "files" the last word, so anything
# that allowlist pulls in — everything under server/, for one — is NOT
# excludable from here. That is why server/.env is kept out by a `!` entry in
# "files" itself, and why scripts/check-package.js exists to assert the result
# rather than trust either mechanism. Shipping a live API token to the registry
# is not an undoable mistake.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

test/
scripts/
.github/
.claude/
*.log

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
